WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.600
ADP tells you what the room usually does.

00:00:03.600 --> 00:00:07.288
OverADP tells you who your roster should draft right now.

00:00:07.938 --> 00:00:13.200
OverADP combines projections, ADP price, VBD and uncertainty.

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:17.800
Then it adds your roster fit.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.390
Every pick changes the board, so OverADP recalculates.

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:27.300
Target Intel identifies the best available target.

00:00:27.300 --> 00:00:31.892
It explains the fit and flags who probably will not make it back.

00:00:32.542 --> 00:00:37.300
Make your pick, and the recommendation changes.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:42.483
It updates for starter needs, scarcity and next-turn availability.

00:00:43.133 --> 00:00:48.100
Our study excluded waivers, trades and lineup changes.

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:52.500
We froze the Week One lineup.

00:00:52.500 --> 00:00:56.739
That isolated the quality of the draft itself.

00:00:57.389 --> 00:01:02.300
Across 1,000 paired historical drafts,

00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:07.300
Target Intel produced a 50.6% top-three rate,

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:11.861
versus 25.7% for ADP-first teams—nearly double.

00:01:12.511 --> 00:01:16.200
That is historical evidence, not a guarantee.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.100
Try five roster-aware picks free.

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:23.355
Unlock your complete draft for $6.99 at OverADP.com.
